WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Dr.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.300
Mario, the prescription is fun!

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:28.660
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.780
I'm Mike.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.680
I'm Sean.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.780
And I'm Sean. Yeah, you have to do the end.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.880
Yeah, yeah. In honor of Joe.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.260
Joe's not here.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.420
I can't lead everyone on to make them expect another voice.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.640
And it's what we've all been waiting for, another Mario game.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.080
The Mario game that I always was like, that can't be a Mario game.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.920
Dr. Mario, right?

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.280
Like, just write to doctor?

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.300
Did he go to school?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.900
Did they give him an honorary PhD for saving the Mushroom Kingdom?

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.020
It's kind of strange that this is like the first thing that he tries to do after Plummer.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.720
Well, here's the real question.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.000
Is Dr.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.160
Mario a different Mario?

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.560
No, it's Mario.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.260
I think it is because if you go into the manual, the first page-

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.180
You think it's a different Mario? No, no, I'm saying just following Smash Brothers logic.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.880
Like, you know, there's Mario and then there's Dr.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.460
Mario. And like, Dr. Mario would just be a skin then, right?

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.800
Like, you would just be a selectable costume for Mario, but he's a totally different character.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.840
However, the manual for this game, first page says,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.520
My name is Dr.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.480
Mario. Hi, everybody.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.560
I'm Mario.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.480
How's it going? Over the last few years, I've been involved in some pretty wild adventures.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.060
Now, believe it or not, I work in the virus research lab at the Mushroom Kingdom Hospital.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.980
Like, what a weird premise to start this game.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:56.540
Wuhan Hospital?

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.560
Is that what he said?

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.240
He said the Mushroom Kingdom Hospital, but-

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.340
Oh. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:11.420
They even have like a little like, little like dialogue between him and not Princess, but Nurse Toadstool.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.500
Dr. Mario, something terrible has happened.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.180
What's wrong, Nurse Toadstool?

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.620
One of the experiments has gone out of control.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.720
The viruses are spreading quickly.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.680
Oh, no. We've got to do something.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.980
I have just developed a new vitamin that should be able to take care of it.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.180
I sure hope this stuff works.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.180
It's like, what's happening?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.700
None of this is like exposition nobody needed, right?

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.600
Well, I'm just glad. It doesn't actually say much.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.060
It does.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:41.880
It teaches you that as long as you take vitamins, you won't have anything to worry about.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.460
But we knew that from Hulk Hogan.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.960
Oh, yeah. Hulk Hogan always told us to take our vitamins.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:53.460
But he never made claims about like, you know, this will explicitly cure this virus.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.900
Yeah. All right.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.720
I understand. Dr.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.500
Mario developed by Nintendo R&D 1.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.060
Do you know any other Nintendo R&D 1 games?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.700
Aren't like all the...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.620
That's like... They're the big dogs.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.180
They're the big dogs in like what way?

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.400
Like that's the... Isn't that like...

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.780
You know, if you make it to like the alpha team, then you're a big dog.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:25.320
And this isn't me just kind of not remembering a specific game that they may have made.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.080
They're not the Mario people?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.800
No, no. So Super Mario Brothers, that's R&D...

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.920
And Legend of Zelda.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.240
That's R&D 4.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.680
Those guys...

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.700
Oh. Those guys just make perfect games.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.940
In fact, in our developer breakdown, we have...

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:48.660
Let's see. R&D 1 made 26 total NES games so far that we've played.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.620
15 skip-its.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.300
8 play-its.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:53.740
3 essentials.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.660
What are the essentials?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.360
Let's see. Metroid.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.140
Okay. Let's see if I can pull up another one real fast.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.220
Duck Hunt. Ah, yes.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.100
And Balloon Fight.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.100
Okay, so I mean, they're still...

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.200
Still doing bangers.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.860
Yeah, they're still doing good stuff.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.660
I guess I already knew this at some point.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.500
And have forgotten because those are all old games.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.200
At least to us.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.740
Right, yeah. What was like the most recent R&D 1 game?

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.220
Shouldn't surprise you, though.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.460
Okay. It was Tetris.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:30.940
Oh, wow. All right.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.720
So they're like, yeah, we have an engine and everything.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.400
We know how to make these puzzle games.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.860
Let's just make our own version of a puzzle game featuring a Nintendo character because

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.260
the licensing on that Russian IP might be a little sketchy.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:50.400
I guess, yeah, there is still a Soviet Union at this point.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:57.220
And I'm sure that they're pretty tough with, you know, their...

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.780
You say they're a litigious group?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.580
I would imagine.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:07.900
You know what? Now I don't really think I know if they could because, you know what?

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.260
This is a rabbit hole.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.200
It's not worth going down.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:11.920
Yes. Dr.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.560
Mario, a puzzle game starring Mario in a lab coat.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.520
But I have to ask you this question.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.320
Are you playing as Mario?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.240
Yeah. I mean, you're...

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.540
Or maybe, like, you're playing as all of the pills.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:30.200
Or, like, he actually just put a bunch of, like, Mexican jumping beans in the pills.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.080
And you're the jumping bean.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.780
Yeah. You can clearly see Dr.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:35.780
Mario on the screen.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:40.260
And you can clearly see him holding what's going to be the next vitamin.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.800
But he does throw it in, too.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:48.340
But then you control, like, where the vitamin lands and, like, turning it and everything.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:57.120
But you could assume that just like how you're playing as, you know, LeBron James in NBA 2K25 or whatever they're called these days.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:03.960
You could assume that, like, you don't just go from playing LeBron to playing as the basketball once the ball has left to hand.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.520
No. That's some... That's only some...

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.500
That only you would say.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.720
Yeah, yeah. Exactly.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.220
No, no. I'm not arguing it.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:17.140
I'm saying that I think I'm agreeing that you do play as Dr.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:22.440
Mario in this game. Probably not the way people wanted to play as Mario in a puzzle game, right?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.340
You probably wanted to do something with jumping or platforming.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.480
But in a way, you're building platforms here.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.620
So there's some element of that.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.600
But it's not...

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.860
It's Mario like we've never seen him before.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.820
Because Mario will have more puzzle games.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.280
But this is his first, like, puzzle game on the NES.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:49.940
Other stuff has been, you know, either arcade-y or as a side-scrolling platformer.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.440
So to have Dr.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:07:01.000
Mario here, it's kind of like, you know, the Mickey Mouse thing for Disney where you're just like, yeah, well, we have a company mascot and he's just going to go do the thing now.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:07.980
Like, it's kind of surprising that they didn't also put him in some of these other Nintendo games like Barker Bill's trick shooting, right?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.620
It could have been Mario's trick shooting.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:14.520
I think they were doing really well not falling into that.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.020
That kind of sounds like a crutch to me.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.800
They're like, oh, let's just put our mascot in everything.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:25.000
And I think they've been doing pretty good staying away from that pattern.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:33.800
But I guess I have to imagine that if this wasn't Mario marketed, that this wasn't going to do very well.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.240
Like, what else?

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:39.080
Like, how else was this going to, like, get players?

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.980
It's a good question.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.860
Here's another Mario question for you.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:50.280
So you throw vitamins and you have to stack a four of the same color in order to clear.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.720
Should it have been vitamins?

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:59.400
Like, isn't, like, mushrooms are what Mario eats to, like, get bigger and stronger.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.040
Should it have been, like, little mushrooms of different colors?

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.740
I think that would be a very different kind of doctor.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:11.920
And maybe they'd have to give it a different name.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:13.960
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.520
Yeah, I don't know.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:25.580
I feel like also mushrooms, while they are simple enough, would be a little too busy of, like, a sprite for that to work here.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:30.240
I think that the pills are just, you know, it's just two squares.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.040
So, as we've said, Mario has apparently received his medical license.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.740
No details provided on that, even in the manual.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.080
Just, I'm a doctor now.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.400
Like, literally just says that.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.840
The objective is to eradicate the viruses from, it's actually cute, the screen.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:53.340
It looks like it's just another one of those Tetris rectangle things, but it is a medicine bottle, like, shape, right?

00:08:53.540 --> 00:09:01.540
So, you're kind of, like, building out the entire, you're filling up the bottle that the person will then drink, right?

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:05.040
Like, first you're getting rid of the virus, and then you're giving the bottle to that person.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.100
You following my lead here?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:15.760
I suppose. I think, you know, the bottle is a little strange if it's actually interacting with the viruses on the side, you know?

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:26.500
Sure, yeah, yeah. I guess they put the, maybe it's like a, you know, like a lab thing, and they're just putting the viruses in there, and then they're clearing them out, and then no one's actually going to drink it or anything.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:33.660
It's just like, this was the cure for this specific virus, because it's made up of three different kinds of virus colors.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.140
There are red, blue, and yellow viruses.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:45.380
You'll know them because they appear to have, like, under a microscope, they're like characters with personalities, and they make silly faces and things.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:56.660
But also, inside the bottle, where you're throwing the vitamins into, you'll see little versions of them with just their faces, just kind of in one continuous, like, two-frame animation loop.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.500
You know, I guess, like, chipping at the player or whatever.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:08.380
So, you have to match four of the same color in a row against those viruses in order to clear them.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:18.420
You can also just clear your own vitamins four in a row, but that's not necessarily helpful, because the only way to get to the next stage is to clear all of the viruses.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:27.940
So, if a virus is blue, you need to stack three of the blue vitamins on top of it or to the side of it in order to clear it.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.320
This is all very true.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.800
I'm only speaking facts here.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.640
That is the way you play the game.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:11:02.620
How did you feel, you know, obviously the thing that they're playing off of here, Tetris, like, it's actually very different, as opposed to what I thought, walking into it, seeing, like, people play it in the past, like, is like, oh, this is just Tetris with less shapes.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.320
Did you have to, like, rewire your brain to do this?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:19.620
It's interesting, because, yeah, it matches the same falling block style gameplay, but because of the match four thing, it winds up being a little more like those Puyo Puyo games, which have now merged with Tetris.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.620
There's Puyo Puyo Tetris games.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:33.140
And the one thing I learned about that was that, like, my brain can't necessarily handle the, you know, like, the stacking nature.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:47.040
Like, oh, I'm going to purposefully make connections that don't connect, because once I drop in this one, it's going to make everything else fall and complete rows and rows of different colors that I had set up previously.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:12:00.280
And I'm sure it's actually, like, a pretty simple-to-gather, like, you know, setup that you need to do of, like, okay, you want to put down three of this and then one of this other one and then three more of this one on this side.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:03.960
Granted, they would have to fall in that order for it to work, so it's easier said than done.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:05.880
You'd have to deal with what the game gives you.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.820
But I still just can never wrap my brain around that.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:15.360
So what I wind up doing instead is what I imagine a lot of, at least the kids at the time were doing, if not most people who still play Dr.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:22.640
Mario, is, you know, you just wind up saying, like, okay, well, how do I get, like, four in front of this virus?

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:27.760
And then everything else can just kind of go over to the side, you know, where the viruses are and are.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.760
I guess I kind of do that.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:37.120
But if you play long enough, like, you'll be able to internalize those patterns more.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.960
But, yeah, no, I'm a pretty basic person when it comes to these kinds of games.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.760
I'm also very bad at Tetris.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:55.860
So I think it's just, like, if you put me under, like, a time, like, a very short, like, several second time limit and try to make patterns with blocks, I'm just not your guy.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.180
But that's basically what I did.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:12.240
Yeah. And you have to remember, too, the reason why I was saying about the once you clear a row, you can have a chain reaction is because any of the vitamins comes in blocks of two.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.700
And it doesn't necessarily guarantee that it's going to be two of the same color.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:21.400
So you might have a yellow and blue vitamin or a yellow, yellow vitamin or a red and blue vitamin.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:27.400
And you always know at least what's coming next as the one that's falling is being prepared to be placed.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:36.060
But you're always just basically playing in the sense of eventually there's going to be capsule fragments after you clear stuff.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.340
And those remain.

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:46.480
So a yellow-blue vitamin that connects to three other blues, only the blue part of that vitamin goes away.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:52.420
And the yellow either continues to fall down the puzzle or stays right where it was if there's nothing holding below it.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:14:02.020
So there becomes this, like, you know, you do have to, especially in the later levels where they stack a lot of viruses inside the bottle screen.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:08.200
You have to think about where these things are going to fall, and that's always going to be my downfall.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.920
Tetris is a game of shapes, you know, so at least I know what the shapes look like.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:18.520
These, because of them just being always two of them, it's a different kind.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.260
It's like how Puyo Puyo, I think, is always either.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.200
It's either always two or always three of them.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:34.480
It's the same thing where, like, you have to think about how you're placing these things because the ones that you're not creating matches for are permanently there now.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:42.060
Like, you're eventually going to have to either clear them or you've made a part of the puzzle that you have essentially, like, locked yourself out of.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:42.880
It's not good.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:56.860
I remember several times playing this that you could just feel the extra time that you just caused yourself by closing off a line of three with a color that you didn't mean to.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:04.680
And now you're going to have to go through several more rotations before you can even get to that part of the puzzle again.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.240
And then hopefully it lines up.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:20.480
I think, like, part of what really got me on this was with Tetris, you know, you kind of start with a blank slate and then any problems that may occur are kind of your fault.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:24.660
But in this game, in the beginning, it's not too bad.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.540
They give you, like, three or four viruses to clear out.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:35.260
But in later levels, like, it's like most of the screen are viruses in whatever pattern.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:48.560
And so you've got to very quickly start thinking about how you want to, even if you can think about how you can combo in the beginning because you already have very little space to work with.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:53.140
Yeah. And even if it was a, you know, like a skill issue for us, right?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.240
And like, oh, well, actually, it's very satisfying if you know what you're doing.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.900
I don't disagree.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:12.500
I think, like, people who can create these chain reactions, that's a very, you know, not only is it a very important part of the game for winning, but it's the most satisfying thing about it is if it happens to you even on accident, you just play it off like, yeah, I always meant to do that.

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.360
You know? Yeah, just like I wrote it up.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:28.540
Exactly. But that's, like, the most fun part because otherwise, as you continue to clear through these levels, we've talked about that they add more viruses into the screen, but also the speed increases.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:36.880
The whole time Mario's up there in the top right, just kind of like some weirdly smug lab supervisor watching over you like, I wouldn't have done that.

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:43.440
And the only saving grace is that the music tracks are awesome.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:50.380
So they're, you know, they're, one of them is the one that I always think of when I think of Dr.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:53.440
Mario, but the other one I just think of as, like, an NES track, and it's great, too.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:56.400
They are, like, right there with Tetris.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:17:06.080
Again, so you have, like, this unique puzzle game thing, right, where it's, like, you need to, just like Tetris, right, you need to know what you're doing in order to, like, be good at the game.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.460
You can't just stack blocks anywhere.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.260
But then also, like, the music in Tetris was great.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.580
The music here is great.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:17.700
So I don't think Nintendo, like, just made a Tetris clone and called it a day.

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:22.680
